 segment grants licenses or provides rights to use portions of its intellectual property portfolio, which include various patent rights useful in the manufacture and sale of wireless products comprising products implementing LTE, and/or OFDMA-based 5G products and derivatives; and grants licenses to use cellular standard-essential patents, including 3G, 4G and 5G for cellular devices. The QSI segment invests in early-stage companies in various industries, including AI, automotive, consumer, enterprise, IoT, and data center, as well as non-marketable and marketable equity securities, and convertible debt instruments. It is also involved in Qualcomm government technologies and data center businesses; and modular businesses that provides software platforms, tools, and cloud-based services that enable developers and enterprises to build, deploy, and scale AI applications across heterogeneous computing environments. QUALCOMM Incorporated was incorporated in 1985 and is headquartered in San Diego, California.","employees":57000,"website":"https://www.qualcomm.com","country":"United States","city":"San Diego","officers":[{"name":"Mr. Cristiano Renno Amon","title":"CEO, President & Director"},{"name":"Mr. Akash  Palkhiwala","title":"Executive VP, CFO & COO"},{"name":"Ms. Ann N. Cathcart Chaplin","title":"Executive VP, General Counsel & Corporate Secretary"}]},"sector_medians":{"fpe":17.44,"tpe":29.99,"ps":4.427,"pfcf":26.07,"peg":1.11,"pb":4.648,"ev_ebitda":18.98,"rev_growth":0.191,"eps_growth":0.356,"eps_growth_fwd":0.2432,"eps_growth_next":0.1809,"div_yield":0,"roe":0.1241,"roa":0.04945,"de":32.8,"gross_margin":0.5312,"op_margin":0.1174,"profit_margin":0.09364,"current_ratio":1.863},"valuation":[{"k":"fpe","label":"Forward P/E","v":14.46,"sector":17.44,"verdict":"Fairly valued"},{"k":"tpe","label":"TTM P/E","v":13.9,"sector":29.99,"verdict":"Undervalued"},{"k":"ps","label":"Price / Sales","v":4.375,"sector":4.427,"verdict":"Fairly valued"},{"k":"pfcf","label":"Price / FCF